Z||000000||mrfixit58||07-22-2000||08:31 AM||||Just had to pass along my good fortune.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Went to the U-Pull-It yard yesterday and got first dibs on a rear-ended  86 GT fast back. I got: a good passenger seat, right rear tail light, left side engine grill, passenger side drip rail, 120 mph speedo and surround, and power trunk solinoid. <P>Unfortunatly, the clowns running the fork lift, destroyed a perfect nose. It had a good passenger side ground effects but I didn't have time to pull it. I also scored a pre-recall trunk lid weather strip in perfect condition from a second and over $5.00 in change!<P>What a country,<BR>Roy<P><BR> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||Phantom Rage||07-23-2000||08:07 PM||||What a shame about that GT, I saw it today.  <P>I believe I met some of your club members, pretty cool guys.  I saw them at the car show held every weekend at the Burger King on Dale Maybry (SP?).  I wish I could have made the show over in Clearwater last week.  <BR>I believe one of the guys went by the name Roy too, drives a white SE.  The other guy had a kinda of Mohawk thing going on. He drove a white GT, with digital gauges, says that it was the original prototype made by Pisa.<BR>Anyway hope to meet you soon, and I am seriously considering joining your club, if time permits  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>By the way I saw some cool cars at the show, ranging from an AMX (model?), GMC Cyclone / Typhoon,and a Pantera, to name a few.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Phantom Rage (edited 07-23-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000002||mrfixit58||07-24-2000||09:53 AM||||Phantom,<P>I'm planning on making the next meeting of the Suncoast Fiero Club. It's the second Wednesday of each month at Autoway Pontiac in St. Pete. If you want specific directions just e-mail me. Hope to see you there!<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
